            "review_title": "Review at Fresh Restaurant & Coffee",
            "review_text": "striped_tiger\nWellington, New Zealand40 contributions\n0\nSurprised at how good the food was\nJun 2017 • Couples\nWe were staying at the hotel and ate here twice - once for dinner and once for lunch. A variety of Vietnamese, western and Mexican food on the menu, plus a cabinet of cakes etc.\nAfter a couple of weeks of Vietnamese food the burger was calling me. It was really really good - well cooked Aussie beef patty, great flavours, easy to eat and not too fancy for its own good. This would easily compare with a good burger in Wellington. And, the cajun potato chunks were perfectly crispy.\nThe fried spring rolls had whole prawns in them with the tail poking out - looked good and also delicious. \nA large range of juices available - come with sugar syrup on the side to sweeten to your own taste.\nStaff were very good.\nInside and outside areas to sit.\nNot super cheap but the food was worth it.\nAccess is up about 6 wide wooden steps from the pavement into the hotel foyer. No ramp.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 23, 2017",
